      "side": 1,
      "message": "When `DataContainsExternalFormat` returns false, we just return `false` as if it doesn\u0027t contain an external format (and presumably if the client doesn\u0027t skip it then, it\u0027ll just fail to be deserialized during regular precompilation so it\u0027s fine).  Should we just simplify `DataContainsExternalFormat` to return the `containsExtFormat` bool directly and have it early out with false in the event of a failure?",
